WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:10.270
This is the debrief for The Reviewer Re-run, where a reviewer must re-create your output files byte for byte, from a clean session.

2
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.850
First, define the analysis set and fit the specified model.

3
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.190
Second, pin every source of randomness.

4
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.670
Third, write outputs and provenance that never change between runs.

5
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.910
The analysis set is every participant with a week12 value.

6
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.260
Change is week12 minus baseline, and arm becomes a factor with Placebo as the reference.

7
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.980
The model adjusts the treatment effect for baseline.

8
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.390
The treatment row, its confidence interval, and n go into a single results row.

9
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:49.530
The audit sample is drawn inside withr::with_seed() with every RNG kind pinned, so the draw is the same in any session, and the caller's random state is left untouched.

10
00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.810
Files are written with row.names = FALSE, and nothing in them depends on the session.

11
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.870
Provenance records the R version, the seed, and the input file's checksum.

12
00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.940
Three mistakes account for most failed attempts.

13
00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:07.720
Calling set.seed() and never restoring the random state changes the caller's stream, and the clean-session check fails.

14
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:13.270
A timestamp in provenance.txt differs on every run, so the reviewer's re-run is not byte-identical.

15
00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:18.560
And keeping rows with a missing week12 value changes the model, which fails the model check.

16
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.490
This solution passes all eight checks.

17
00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:28.550
The validator self-test runs this exact code against every one of them, so what you see here is what the boss grades.

18
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.490
Your own solution can look different.

19
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.850
What matters is that it passes the same checks.
